<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fraga</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fraga is a town in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huesca">Huesca</a> in Aragon, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cinca">Cinca</a> River. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was a Muslim stronghold where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon">Alfonso I of Aragon</a> suffered a fatal defeat in 1134, and it was finally taken by the Christians in 1149. In October 1936 the anarchist Regional Defence <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-aragon">Council of Aragon</a> was first set up there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fraga.jpg" alt="Fraga" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ecelan · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fraga_-_Vista_general_con_iglesia_de_San_Pedro.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
